s in vivo</article-title><source>Nat. Struct. Mol. Biol.</source><year>2005</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>847</fpage><lpage>854</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16142245</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Neidle</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Parkinson</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Telomere maintenance as a target for anticancer drug discovery</article-title><source>Nat. Rev. Drug Disc.</source><year>2002</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>383</fpage><lpage>393</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dexheimer</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fry</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurley</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Neidle</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Balasubramanian</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA quadruplexes and gene regulation</article-title><source>Quadruplex Nucleic Acids.</source><year>2006</year><comment>RSC Publishing, Cambridge, UK, pp. 180&#x02013;207</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Siddiqui-Jain</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Grand</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bearss</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurley</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Direct evidence for a G-quadruplex in a promoter region and its targeting with a small molecule to repress <italic>c-MYC</italic> transcription</article-title><source>Proc. Natl Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>2002</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>11593</fpage><lpage>11598</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12195017</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cogoi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Quadrifoglio</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Xodo</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>G-rich oligonucleotide inhibits the binding of a nuclear protein to the Ki-<italic>ras</italic> promoter and strongly reduces cell growth in human carcinoma pancreatic cells</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>2004</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>2512</fpage><lpage>2523</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14992588</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bejugam</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sewitz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Shirude</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Shahid</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Balasubramanian</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trisubstituted Isoalloxazines as a new class of G-quadruplex binding ligands: small molecule regulation of c-kit oncogene expression</article-title><source>J. Am. Chem. Soc.</source><year>2007</year><volume>129</volume><fpage>12926</fpage><lpage>12927</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17918848</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huppert</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><